  "description": "Our newest model, the Sunliner, combines the Prospector's geometry and generous tire clearance with the Stargazer's high-end tubeset—all optimized for flat bars. A massive front triangle for extra framebag volume, and all the rack mounts you need for any adventure.\n\nOur titanium frame sets use custom multi-butted, cold-formed oversized 3Al-2.5V tubing paired with a chromoly steel fork. The result is a frame that's approximately two pounds lighter than its steel counterpart, with the corrosion resistance and fatigue life that make titanium a true forever material. Same geometry, same rack and fender mounts, same ride-anywhere capability.\n\nWe've been riding these frames in production and prototype form for several years now, and it's the bike we find ourselves reaching for more than any other for both loaded touring and swoopy trail riding. If you appreciate the lighter weight, corrosion resistance, and dreamy ride quality that titanium offers, then the titanium version of your favorite Tumbleweed is a great option.\n\nWe order titanium frames in occasional, very limited production runs.\n\nGeometry is identical to steel Sunliner (with UDH) signature build with Eagle 90. As always, complete builds are customizable.\n\n3Al-2.5V multi butted titanium tubing, ovalized top tube and down tube\n\nFrameset includes titanium frame with steel fork, seat clamp, front and rear thru axles\n\nTi frame saves approximately 2lbs over the steel frame\n\nBrushed bare titanium finish with dark midnight logos and a matching dark midnight steel fork (same fork that comes with the steel frameset)\n\n29x3.0” or 27.5x3.0” tire clearance with machined titanium chainstay yoke\n\n31.6mm seatpost (compatible with internally routed dropper posts)\n\n44mm headtube for ZS44 upper headset cups and EC44 lower cups, 30mm crown race with stock fork\n\nThreaded bosses for full size racks and fenders front and rear, three sets of bottle bosses on main triangle, triple bottle bosses on each fork leg\n\n148x12mm frame spacing and 110x15mm fork spacing\n\n160/180mm flat mount disc brakes front and rear\n\n1x drivetrain specific frame, 38t max chainring with 55mm chainline",
